                <pb facs="0323" n="263" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg263"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Eustis to Mr. Uhl</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Embassy of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-06-12"><hi rendition="#italic">June 12, 1895</hi></date>.
                        (Received June 24).</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 315.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your dispatch No. 428, of May 24, with reference to expenses incurred on
                    account of Mr. Bray. In compliance with your instruction, I have this day drawn
                    upon the Secretary of State for the sum of $129.02, amount expended by me, and
                    also for the sum of $1.72, amount lost by exchange. I inclose herewith my
                    accounts for the same.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. B. Eustis</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
